menu "FNK0099 probe"
    config FNK0099_HID_PROBE
        bool "Build the composite keyboard/mouse HID probe"
        default n
        depends on !FNK0099_MSC_PROBE
        help
            Inspect HID interfaces and report descriptors. Input capture is
            enabled only by an explicit UART command and expires after 30 seconds.

    config FNK0099_MSC_PROBE
        bool "Build the USB MSC probe instead of the SFC HID probe"
        default n
        help
            Select the dedicated USB card reader probe. File creation requires
            an explicit UART command. Existing files are not overwritten and
            automatic formatting is disabled.

    config FNK0099_SFC_ROOT_PORT_POWER_MS
        int "Uptime at which the SFC host first powers the USB root port (ms, 0 = at install)"
        default 1150
        range 0 5000
        depends on !FNK0099_HID_PROBE && !FNK0099_MSC_PROBE
        help
            A UIAPduino SFC that is already attached at power-on or across an EN
            reset fails its first enumeration when the host starts it about
            0.6 s after reset, and then stops answering until it is re-plugged.
            Keeping the root port unpowered until this uptime lets the first
            enumeration succeed (1150 ms validated on 2026-11-18; see
            docs/sfc-troubleshooting.md). Devices plugged in later enumerate as
            before. 0 restores powering the port at usb_host_install().
endmenu
